 "description": "Retrieve the full public profile for a username, including skills, experiences, projects, `services` (what they offer with prices: name, price in whole currency units or null for \"ask\", currency, per job/hour/day/visit/session/month, from = starting price, note), `licence` (a registration number Foundaree's admin looked up on its public register, e.g. a doctor's NMC number: body, number, checkedAt; only once verified, and then \"licence\" is also in `verifiedBy`), and the phone, WhatsApp and contact email (`phone`, `whatsapp`, `contactEmail`) when the person made them public. `workProof`, when at least one kind is proven, is a count, not a score: \"Proof: `proven` of `total`\" over GitHub, website and LinkedIn (LinkedIn has no proof yet), with the facts of each proven one: `github` (public facts of a GitHub account they proved is theirs by signing in with it: repos, stars, followers, top languages, last push, and when Foundaree read them) and `website` (their website links back to this profile). `person.updatedAt` is when they last edited the profile. Returns structured JSON with `success`, `found` and `person` fields. Each answer has two views: the text content is the JSON described above, and the structured content is a profile-card list (`people`, `total`, `query`). In apps that support MCP Apps (ChatGPT, Claude) the cards render as Foundaree profile cards. A person with `foundareeRole` (\"founder\" or \"team\") is part of Foundaree's own team; only Foundaree sets it.",
 "execution": {
  "taskSupport": "forbidden"
 },
